# D10 mock — /stateless (events). Contract: #37732 (auth + H/E), #37733 (semantics).
# The three-byte sequence "\nE " separates events; continuation lines carry one
# extra leading space. Authorization MAC = AES-CMAC(agent-key, canonical-request).

### REQUEST
POST /stateless HTTP/1.1
Host: 127.0.0.1:27840
protocol-version: 1
Authorization: Wazuh 001:1784311282:4b88d9235ea1a109d617f27f604918ea
Content-Type: application/octet-stream
Content-Length: 189

H {"wazuh":{"agent":{"id":"001"}}}
E 1:/var/log/syslog:sshd: Accepted publickey for root
E 1:/var/log/auth.log:session opened for user root
E v:vulnerability-scanner:{"cve":"CVE-2024-1234"}

### RESPONSE (accepted — empty body)
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
Content-Length: 0

### RESPONSE (payload agent-id != authenticated id, or malformed batch)
HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request
Content-Type: application/json

{"error":"Invalid event batch","code":400}

### RESPONSE (bad/expired/absent MAC — generic)
HTTP/1.1 401 Unauthorized
Content-Type: application/json

{"error":"Invalid client authentication","code":401}

### RESPONSE (back-pressure)
HTTP/1.1 503 Service Unavailable
Retry-After: 2
Content-Type: application/json

{"error":"Service temporarily unavailable","code":503}
